# Determinism (PLAN §36). The fixtures and the golden snapshots are compared as raw bytes,
# so a checkout must not rewrite their line endings per platform. GitHub's Windows runners
# carry core.autocrlf=true by default, which turns every LF blob in the index into CRLF on
# disk; a snapshot then differs from the bytes the engine writes and the comparison fails
# for packaging reasons rather than for the determinism it exists to probe.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to the index's LF for the patterns the determinism suite
# reads, on every platform. The index blobs are already LF (verified with
# `git ls-files --eol`), so nothing is renormalized and no tracked file changes today —
# this only stops a Windows checkout from rewriting what it receives.

*.golden text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
